First Author: Peyster
Title: An automated computational image analysis pipeline for histological grading of cardiac allograft rejection
Source number: 58  ￼

Very short summary: This multi-center US study developed an automated computational image analysis pipeline (CACHE-Grader) using support vector machines (SVM) and 154 hand-crafted quantitative histological features from endomyocardial biopsy slides to grade cardiac allograft rejection. Five key findings were: (1) 2,472 biopsy slides from 546 heart transplant recipients across 3 major US centers were included; (2) statistical feature selection identified optimal SVM models using 2 features for binary (M1) and 15 features for four-grade (M2) rejection grading; (3) CACHE-Grader achieved 65.9% overall agreement with the grade of record, meeting non-inferiority to expert human pathologists (60.7%); (4) performance was nearly identical across internal (66.1%) and external validation sets (65.8%); and (5) CACHE-Grader demonstrated superior sensitivity for high-grade rejection compared to human pathologists (74.4% vs 39.5%). Figures 1–6 and Tables 1–4 were directly used for this extraction.  ￼

