	•	Section 3 Comments/Quotes: CACHE-Grader applied interpretable, biologically inspired, hand-crafted feature extraction to digitized H&E-stained endomyocardial-biopsy slides. From 154 quantitative histological features, the authors used outcome-based statistical ranking: Wilcoxon rank-sum selection for the binary model and t-test ranking for the four-grade model; final SVMs used 2 and 15 features, respectively. ehab241.pdf The models were locked after training and tested at two geographically separate external centres, with grades assigned by pathologists serving as the reference standard and independent pathologists used for comparative re-grading. ehab241.pdf Major uncertainty: The authors compared several linear classifiers and optimized the number of selected features, but conventional SVM hyperparameter tuning—such as kernel, C, or class-weight optimization—is not described; therefore, hyperparameter tuning is coded Not Reported rather than Yes.  ￼

