	•	Section 4 Comments/Quotes: The training cohort consisted of 911 slides randomly selected from UPenn. The complete held-out validation cohort contained 1,447 slides, comprising 395 internal-validation slides and 1,052 external-validation slides from OSU and UH. ehab241.pdf The investigators deliberately enriched the cohort with 2R/3R biopsies—approximately 20% versus 8% in routine practice—to provide adequate representation of clinically important high-grade rejection. ehab241.pdf Preprocessing included stain deconvolution, K-means tissue segmentation, focus detection, automated HistoQC assessment, and normalization of some features by tissue-compartment size. Source code was made publicly available. ehab241.pdf Major uncertainties: Class imbalance was addressed through dataset-level enrichment, not through reported SMOTE, weighted loss, cost-sensitive SVM training, or resampling within the training algorithm. The paper does not describe conventional missing-value imputation. Slides failing technical quality control were excluded, which is a QC-exclusion procedure rather than missing-data imputation. Test Size = 1447 refers to the composite held-out validation set. The strictly geographically external subset was 1,052 slides.  ￼

